  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>26000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is followed for the decomposition of compound&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>.&nbsp;The activation energy for the reaction is ____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;[nearest integer]</p><p>(Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "216",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>Ae</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>RT</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>12</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>26000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>Ea</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>26000</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ea</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>216</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>164</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence,the activation energy of the given&nbsp;reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>216</mn><mi>KJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mn>1</mn><mrow/></msub></mrow></msup></math></p>"
